+  <h2 id="s1">1. Status stepper — 🐛 B1</h2>
+  <div class="card bug">
+    <span class="badge b-bug">🐛 BUG</span> <strong>Status stepper escapes its card on mobile &lt;768px — regression of #631 fix #2</strong>
+    <p class="muted">Affects: application detail page — live pipeline, rejected, and auto-closed steppers (all share the rail pattern).</p>
+    <table>
+      <tr><th>Viewport</th><th>Stepper left</th><th>Stepper right</th><th>Width</th><th>First stop "Submitted"</th></tr>
+      <tr><td>320×568</td><td><strong>-84</strong></td><td>404</td><td>489</td><td>starts at x=-84 (off-screen)</td></tr>
+      <tr><td>360×800</td><td><strong>-64</strong></td><td>424</td><td>489</td><td>clipped left</td></tr>
+      <tr><td>390×844</td><td><strong>-49</strong></td><td>439</td><td>489</td><td>clipped left</td></tr>
+      <tr><td>768×1024 (md)</td><td>63 ✓</td><td>616</td><td>553</td><td>fits — <code>md:flex-wrap</code> engages</td></tr>
+    </table>
+    <p><strong>Vision confirmation</strong> (screenshot 30, 320px): <em>"Only the tail fragment '…ed' is visible; the rest of the pill is scrolled/clipped outside the left edge… the final visible pill also runs past the right edge."</em></p>
+    <p><strong>Root cause:</strong> <code>application_detail.gleam:370-374</code> wraps the stepper in <code>flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 justify-center lg:justify-end</code>. The stepper root (<code>status_stepper.gleam</code> <code>view_pipeline</code>: <code>flex items-center gap-2 overflow-x-auto w-full</code>) is a flex item with default <code>min-width:auto</code> — it refuses to shrink below its content's intrinsic width (~553px), so <code>w-full</code> loses, the block grows to ~489px and <code>justify-center</code> centers the overflow symmetrically (clipped on BOTH edges). The rail does scroll internally (scrollW 553 vs clientW 489) but is never constrained to the parent width.</p>
+    <p><strong>Suggested fix (for your decision):</strong> add <code>min-w-0</code> to the stepper root (or the flex item in <code>application_detail</code>), so <code>overflow-x-auto</code> engages at the parent's width.</p>
