+## Bug (🐛)
+
+### B1. Status stepper escapes its card on mobile (regression of #631 fix #2)
+- **Where:** Application detail page (`/vacancies/:vid/applications/:id`) — live pipeline
+  stepper AND rejected stepper AND auto-closed stepper (all share the rail pattern).
+- **Measured (DOM):** at 320×568: stepper container left=-84, right=404, w=489 (viewport 320);
+  first stop "Submitted" starts at x=-84 (off-screen left). At 390×844: left=-49, right=439.
+  Rejected stepper: left=-52, right=442 (390). Rail internal scrollW=553 vs clientW=489 —
+  the rail DOES scroll, but the whole block is 489–495px wide inside a 288px content column.
+- **Vision confirmation:** screenshot 30 (320): "only the tail fragment '…ed' is visible" of
+  the first pill; last pill clipped at right edge; row behaves like "a scrolled horizontal
+  strip rather than a row that fits the 320px width".
+- **Root cause:** `application_detail.gleam:370-374` wraps the stepper in
+  `flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 justify-center lg:justify-end`. The stepper root
+  (`status_stepper.gleam` `view_pipeline`: `flex items-center gap-2 overflow-x-auto w-full`)
+  is a flex item with default `min-width:auto` — it refuses to shrink below its content's
+  intrinsic width (~553px), so `w-full` loses, the block grows to 489px and `justify-center`
+  centers the overflow symmetrically (both edges clipped). The #631 fix made the rail
+  scrollable but never constrained it to the parent width. Fix needs `min-w-0` on the
+  stepper root (or the flex item in application_detail).
+- **Repro:** open any application detail (demo or live) at ≤390px; the first 1–2 status
+  stops are clipped off-screen on the left, last stop clipped on the right; no visual
+  affordance that the row is horizontally scrollable.
+- **Impact:** user cannot see/confirm the applicant's current status step without
+  discovering the hidden scroll; "Submitted" and "Reviewing" steps unreadable.
+- Classification: 🐛 (functional — clipped content on the primary status surface).
+
